Refs ed3c/soodles#55

This atom prevents a cloud Session from crossing into the local Git/Noodle reconciliation route after provider delivery.

Behavior:

- claim shape selects the already-observed Session route: cloud omits `control_root`; local includes it;
- cloud `landing advance` resolves only from fresh exact merge, Issue closure, runtime and provider-main evidence;
- if main advanced, a complete merge-to-main comparison is required;
- cloud resolution invokes neither shell Git, runtime doctor nor Noodle;
- local claims retain the existing binary, fetch, fast-forward and cleanup boundary;
- a completed legacy checkpoint may migrate local → cloud only with fixed provider identity, changed external verifier, complete writes, no execution envelope and no real cleanup intent;
- migration emits no provider write and requires fresh connector readback before resolution;
- cloud → local migration and cloud invocation of `reconcile` refuse.

Local evidence:

- 113 discovered unit tests passed with no skips;
- canonical acceptance passed with pinned Noodle v0.1.19;
- cloud controls assert no `fetch_main` or `runtime_check` call;
- skill structural validation passed.

The local checkout lacked two historical N-class result files added after its base, so its clean local commit tree differs only at those files. This PR commit was constructed on current provider main `008d5e98e092f3c13a04a501188dc41cb73094c7`; exact-head Actions is the authoritative candidate run.

issue.body:
## Intent

Correct the route mismatch exposed by Issue #53: a ChatGPT cloud Session selected the GitHub connector / Actions path, completed provider merge and closure readback, then the landing owner incorrectly required the local-only shell Git and Noodle reconciliation path.

Cloud delivery must terminate from fresh provider state. Local delivery must retain Git fast-forward, worktree ownership and Noodle cleanup. The owner must not silently cross routes after Session entry.

## Minimal design

Use claim shape, not another policy flag:

- common claim identity retains repository, Issue, PR, head/tree/base, runtime run/attempt, PR head ref (the existing `worktree` field), and verifier digest;
- a local claim additionally contains `control_root` and may contain `execution_envelope`;
- a cloud claim omits `control_root` and cannot contain `execution_envelope`.

The supervisor-selected Session path supplies the matching claim shape. No CLI probe, browser, Codex CLI, Noodle binary or shell Git is required for the cloud route.

## Cloud terminal contract

After this checkpoint offered merge and close exactly once, fresh connector readback must prove:

- exact repository, Issue, PR, candidate commit/tree and successful exact-head runtime run/job;
- PR merged with the exact ordered base/candidate parents and candidate tree;
- Issue closed with `state_reason=completed`;
- provider `main` equals the merge commit, or a complete comparison proves the merge commit is an ancestor of current main.

Then `landing advance` may persist `phase=resolved`, `classification=RESOLVED`, a cloud/provider reconciliation receipt, and `next=null`. It must not inspect a control root, invoke Git/Noodle, manufacture a worktree or emit another provider request.

## Local contract

A claim containing `control_root` keeps the existing behavior: provider closure advances to local reconciliation; `landing reconcile` validates origin/clean identity, fetches/fast-forwards main and delegates actual resource cleanup to Noodle. A cloud claim must refuse the local reconcile entry.

## Existing checkpoint migration

A corrected externally selected verifier may migrate a completed legacy local-shaped checkpoint to the cloud claim shape only when:

- merge and closure readbacks were already adopted;
- `writes_offered == ["merge", "close"]`;
- provider/candidate/run/head-ref identities are unchanged;
- verifier digest changes;
- no execution envelope is present;
- any existing cleanup intent is absent or the already-observed no-op form.

Migration emits no provider request and returns the exact fresh provider-readback operation. It cannot migrate cloud to local, drop a real cleanup intent, change subject identity or resolve without fresh connector evidence.

This permits the preserved #53 and #51 checkpoints to complete without replaying merge/close or requiring shell Git.

## Controls

Positive controls:

1. a native cloud claim resolves from fresh provider readback without calling Git, runtime check or Noodle;
2. a later main head resolves only with exact merge-to-main comparison evidence;
3. a completed legacy checkpoint migrates local → cloud and then resolves;
4. an ordinary local checkpoint still requires the binary and existing reconcile path.

Planted negatives refuse:

- missing/malformed merge, Issue closure, runtime or main ancestry evidence;
- cloud claim plus execution envelope or local reconcile invocation;
- route migration before both writes/readbacks complete;
- migration changing provider/candidate/run/head-ref identity;
- local → cloud migration with a real cleanup intent;
- cloud → local migration.

## Evidence and delivery

Use the existing externally selected landing owner for this Issue. Candidate tests and Actions are non-authorizing. Preserve #53/#51 checkpoints and provider writes. After this fix is independently merged, migrate their verifier/route and consume fresh GitHub readback; do not rerun their evaluations or merge/close operations.
